# =============================================================================
# Automotive Retail Performance Intelligence (ARPI) — .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# Two rules matter more than everything else in this file:
#
#   1. NEVER COMMIT SECRETS.
#      Credentials live in environment variables and in a local, untracked
#      `.env`. The only committed environment file is `.env.example`, which
#      contains placeholder values and no real password.
#
#   2. NEVER COMMIT FULL GENERATED DATASETS.
#      The synthetic dataset is reproducible from a seed, so the repository
#      stores the *generator*, not its multi-megabyte output. A small, capped,
#      deliberately committed sample lives in `data/sample/` so the repository
#      is reviewable without running anything.
#
# Everything below is grouped by concern. Prefer adding a new commented section
# over appending an unexplained pattern at the bottom.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local environment
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All `.env` variants are ignored. `.env.example` is the tracked template and is
# explicitly negated below — keep that negation after the broad patterns.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Ad-hoc credential files that occasionally appear in data work.
.pgpass
*.pgpass
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
credentials.json


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Railway deployment state and generated output
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE THE SHAPE OF THIS SECTION. `.railway/` is NOT ignored, and must not be:
# `.railway/railway.ts` is the source-controlled Infrastructure as Code
# declaration and is the whole point of the directory. Only the CLI's own local
# state is excluded — that file records the linked project and environment for
# whoever ran `railway link`, and `railway login` can write a token beside it.
#
# The same applies to `deployment/railway/`: every file in it is deliberately
# tracked. Ignoring a deployment configuration directory to be safe would make
# the deployment unreviewable, which is the opposite of safe.
.railway/state.json
.railway/*.local.json
.config/railway/

# Machine-readable results the bootstrap, verification and audit tools write into
# the working directory when run by hand or by the workflow. Non-secret by
# construction — every one passes through the redactor — but they are outputs of a
# run against one account, not repository content.
/bootstrap.json
/dry-run.json
/verification.json
/lighthouse/
/portfolio/playwright-report-remote/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Installed Node dependencies
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `portfolio/.gitignore` already covers the website's tree. This covers the
# repository root, which now carries a package.json for the Railway deployment
# tooling. The lockfiles at both levels are tracked.
/node_modules/
node_modules/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python virtual environments
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode, build output, and packaging metadata
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
sdist/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/
pip-wheel-metadata/
MANIFEST


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test, type-check, and lint caches
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.tox/
.nox/
.cache/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Coverage output
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
coverage.json
htmlcov/
nosetests.xml


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated datasets (rule 2)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Full generator output is reproducible from the configured random seed. The
# directories themselves are kept in the tree via a tracked `.gitkeep`.
data/raw/**
!data/raw/.gitkeep
data/external/**
!data/external/.gitkeep

# DELIBERATELY TRACKED — do not add `data/sample/` to this file.
# `data/sample/` holds the small, row-capped, 100% synthetic extract that makes
# the repository reviewable without executing the pipeline. It is committed on
# purpose. The negations below are redundant today and exist as a guard rail so
# that a future broad `data/` pattern cannot silently drop the sample.
!data/sample/
!data/sample/**


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database dumps and restore artifacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: plain `*.sql` is intentionally NOT ignored — `sql/**` is source code and
# must stay tracked. Only compressed and binary dump formats are excluded.
*.dump
*.backup
*.sql.gz
*.sql.bz2
*.sql.zip
*.pgdump


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log
*.log.*
pip-log.txt


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Power BI
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only Power BI *temporary* and *packaged-visual* artifacts are ignored.
#
# DELIBERATELY TRACKED — do not add these to this file:
#   *.pbip                  Power BI project (source-controlled) entry point
#   *.Report/               PBIP report source folder (JSON, diffable)
#   *.SemanticModel/        PBIP semantic model source folder (TMDL, diffable)
#   powerbi/measures/*.dax  DAX measure definitions kept as reviewable text
# PBIP source directories are the entire reason Power BI work can live in git;
# ignoring them would make the semantic model unreviewable.
~$*.pbix
*.pbix.tmp
*.pbix.bak
*.pbiviz

# Machine-specific Power BI Desktop project state, documented at
# https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/developer/projects/projects-dataset.
# These are per-user and per-machine, and `localSettings.json` in particular can carry a
# data-source path or a resolved connection for the person who last opened the project.
# Nothing here is part of the semantic model definition.
**/.pbi/localSettings.json
**/.pbi/cache.abf
**/.pbi/unappliedChanges.json
# Belt and braces: the two files above are the documented ones, and this catches a cache
# or backup that a future Desktop release adds beside them.
**/.pbi/*.abf


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Excel and Office temporary files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
~$*.xlsx
~$*.xlsm
~$*.xlsb
~$*.docx
~$*.pptx
*.xlk


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Jupyter
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
profile_default/
ipython_config.py


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and IDE metadata
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.spyderproject
.spyproject
.ropeproject


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating-system metadata
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Explicitly NOT ignored (documentation of intent, not active patterns)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The following are tracked and must remain tracked:
#
#   pyproject.toml                        single source of Python tool config
#   .env.example                          template with placeholder values only
#   sql/**                                all DDL/DML source, including *.sql
#   docs/**                               architecture, ADRs, dictionary, KPIs
#   config/*.yaml                         profiles (never contain a password)
#   data/sample/**                        capped synthetic sample extract
#   powerbi/measures/*.dax                DAX measure source
#   *.pbip, *.Report/, *.SemanticModel/   Power BI project source
